#: src/reference/community-plugins.md:8
msgid "The GitHub sbt Organization"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/community-plugins.md:10
msgid ""
"The [sbt organization](https://github.com/sbt) is available for use by any "
"sbt plugin. Developers who contribute their plugins into the community "
"organization will still retain control over their repository and its access. "
"The goal of the sbt organization is to organize sbt software into one "
"central location."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/community-plugins.md:16
msgid ""
"A side benefit to using the sbt organization for projects is that you can "
"use gh-pages to host websites under the https://www.scala-sbt.org domain."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/community-plugins.md:19
msgid ""
"The [sbt autoplugin giter8 template](https://github.com/sbt/sbt-"
"autoplugin.g8) is a good place to start. This sets up a new sbt plugin "
"project appropriately. The generated `README` includes a summary of the "
"steps for publishing a new community plugin."
msgstr ""

